# Files that must never enter the Docker build context (issue #26, step 2).
# The Dockerfile only copies named files today, so this is a second line of defence: it still
# protects us if someone later writes "COPY . .". (non-negotiable #2: never ship .env).
# tests/test_container_image.py and scripts/container_check.sh verify these rules.
#
# .dockerignore patterns are anchored at the build-context root: ".env*" would NOT match
# "scripts/.env". "**/" makes a pattern match at any depth. Don't add "!" exceptions (a test
# forbids them): they can silently bring a secret back in.

# Secrets and local configuration (also catches .env.local, .env.canary ...), at any depth
**/.env*

# Terraform state and variable files can hold secrets; saved plans too
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfvars.json
**/tfplan

# Local environments, version control, caches, scratch databases
venv/
.git/
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache/
audit_log.db

# Local-only business notes, agent settings, old code
private/
.claude/
depreciated/

# Not part of the runtime image
evals/
tests/
infra/
